  "description": "The temple of the god S\u00een, Eki\u0161nugal (\u201cHouse of the Great Light\u201d), was located in the Kullab district of Babylon, in the eastern half of the inner city. According to the Babylonian topographical text Tintir = Babylon Tablet IV, it was one of four temples in that part of Babylon. The temple is mentioned in Old Babylonian Period texts and was (re)built by the Old Babylonian king Ab\u012b-\u0113\u0161uh (r. ca. 1711\u20131684 BC) and the Neo-Babylonian ruler Nebuchadnezzar II (r. 604\u2013562 BC). The temple survived into the Hellenistic Period.",
